note: jsonreport — read a typed JSON file and answer questions about it:
note: `jsonreport FILE [MIN_SCORE]`

include "std/text"

a author has name as text, email as maybe text
a post has title as text, tags as list of text, writer as author, score as decimal
a feed has posts as list of post

let path be (maybe item 1 of the arguments) otherwise "feed.json"
let floor be (decimal from ((maybe item 2 of the arguments) otherwise "0")) otherwise 0.0

let doc be (read file path) otherwise ""
let loaded be a feed from json doc
if loaded has no value:
    fail "{path} is not a feed document"

let f be value of loaded
say "{length of f's posts} posts, showing those scoring at least {(fixed_decimal with floor, 1)}"

let kept be an empty list of post
for each p in f's posts:
    if p's score is at least floor:
        add p to kept

for each p in reversed (sorted kept by score):
    let who be (p's writer's email) otherwise p's writer's name
    say "{(fixed_decimal with p's score, 1)}  {p's title}  <{who}>  [{p's tags joined with \", \"}]"

note: the same records serialise back out, in key order, ready to write
let summary be a feed with posts kept
write summary as json to file "kept.json"
say "wrote kept.json"
